6. `mtc-keymaster/read-config/config.server` — commented-out
   example entry.
7. `socket-level-wrapper-MQC/draft-page-mqc-protocol-00.md` —
   §10.5 rewrite, §11 list addition, §12.4 paragraph.

## Out of scope (deliberately deferred)

- **Active revocation push** (the log proactively notifying
  cached verifiers of new revocations).  MTC's design is
  pull-only; push semantics would require new wire format and
  long-lived subscriptions.  Operators who need
  near-real-time revocation set `mqc-revoked-cache-ttl-sec` low
  (e.g., 60 s) and accept the load.
- **Soft-fail with grace window** (treat first query failure as
  "warn but allow", second as "abort").  Adds state, complicates
  diagnostics.  Not justified for v0; can revisit if the
  fail-closed default produces too many false-positive aborts in
  practice.
- **Per-peer revocation policy** (different policies for
  different cert_index values).  Same effect achievable by
  segmenting peers across deployments; not worth the
  configuration surface in v0.
